# Soma News (110+; Google News since 127). Bugs Boss found: empty bullets, related-link tails, sideways scrolling,
# the drop capital's spacing; in 135, white status-bar icons on the cream paper, Reuters' headline read twice, CNBC's
# "watch now" video promos.
# A clean start: no shade or dialog left by an earlier walk.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key BACK
key HOME
launch dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.news.NewsActivity
# The reader's controls appear about 3 s after a fresh start (timed on Fold8), but the 131 walk missed Refresh at 6 s.
wait 10000
# No Refresh here: twenty walks a day each fetching all of Google News helped get the network held back
# (2026-10-22). The reader refreshes by itself when its stream is over an hour old; tap ↻ in a walk only for a
# change to fetching.
wait 8000
expect Top stories
expect Technology
shot stream-cover-new-stories-pill-clear-of-chips
# Look: the clock, signal and battery are drawn DARK on the cream paper (135: white, unseen).
shot status-icons-dark-on-paper
# A refresh started just before scrolling down lands while he is down the stream: its new stories must wait behind
# the pill, not push the stream under the tap (175: 'Show 20 more' opened a Politico story).
tap Refresh
scrollto Show 20 more
wait 1500
scrollto Show 20 more
shot before-show-more
tap Show 20 more
wait 800
# The tap leaves the stream where it was, the list opening below (not back at the top of the section).
shot after-show-more
scrollto Show less
shot topic-expanded
# Back to the top: the chips row scrolls with the stream.
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
tap Technology
wait 800
shot jumped-to-technology
# Open a story under Technology: the whole article loads (or the honest "read it there" fallback).
swipe 0.5 0.7 0.5 0.5 300
tap 0.5 0.45
wait 6000
absent Getting the whole story
absent Related stories
absent Read more
absent watch now
absent STREAM NOW
# Look: dark status icons here too, and the headline once only (not again as the first line of the story).
shot article
key BACK
# Back keeps him in the stream.
expect SOMA
fold open
rotate landscape
wait 1500
shot stream-landscape
# Back to the top first: turning keeps the scroll, and the 13115c4c1 walk's tap landed on an empty left page
# lower down. The first spread's left page is the lead story (a picture, or its headline in words).
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.9 300
wait 800
tap 0.25 0.45
wait 6000
shot book
rotate portrait
[phone] Check the top bar sits clear of Samsung's status strip on the cover screen and unfolded.
[phone] Swipe system Back from an article (back to the stream), then from the stream (back to home).
[phone] Open three top stories from different publishers: each shows the whole article, not only its headline (Boss, 2026-10-22: in 130 none loaded, because Google had blocked the phone's network after the hourly burst of lookups).
[phone] The status bar's clock, signal and battery show dark on the reader's paper, on the cover screen and unfolded (they were white and unseen until 131).
[phone] Open a Reuters story and a CNBC story: the headline shows once (not again as the story's first line), no "watch now"/"STREAM NOW" video promos or their pictures, and the status bar's clock and icons are dark on the cream paper (135: white).
[phone] On cellular (off Wi-Fi), open five top stories from different publishers: the NYT, BBC, Guardian, NPR, CNBC or Fox ones open as whole articles (found on the publisher's own feed, nothing asked of Google); a Reuters or AP one says it didn't give the whole story here, and 'Read it there' opens it in the browser. Nothing says Google is holding the network back after opening them (2026-10-23: Google's 429 on the cellular address).
